<title>USA: Align-Rite buys TEMIC unit.</title>
<headline>Align-Rite buys TEMIC unit.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Align-Rite International Inc said Wednesday it had bought the photomask manufacturing business unit of TEMIC, a division of Daimler-Benz AG.</p>
<p>Align-Rite and TEMIC also said they had struck a long-term alliance and supply deal.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Align-Rite is based in Los Angles. TEMIC is based in Heilbronn, Germany.</p>
<p>Last year TEMIC's photomask demand increased to about 10 million marks, the companies said in a joint statement.</p>
